Description: Adapt the DANOS patch stack to keepalived 2.4.3 after the rebase from 2.2.0.
 
 - _HAVE_FIB_ROUTING_ no longer exists; the guards around track_route code
   would have compiled it out silently. Removed with their #endif.
 - vrrp->vmac_flags is now part of vrrp->flags; nopreempt is the
   VRRP_FLAG_NOPREEMPT bit.
 - The num_script_if_fault counter became fault flags: trackers use
   set_fault()/down_instance()/try_up_instance() with VRRP_FAULT_FL_TRACKER;
   a VMAC that cannot be brought up at MASTER sets
   VRRP_FAULT_FL_INTERFACE_DOWN.
 - Parser handlers use current_vrrp: in 2.4 the instance being parsed is not
   yet on vrrp_data->vrrp, so list_last_entry() returned a bogus instance
   and track_pathmon crashed the config test (track_route wrote through the
   same bad pointer).
 - vrrp_sync_backup() gained a resign argument; the state-transition table
   uses a wrapper keeping resign=false.
 - vrrp_snmp_check_for_daemon() uses the 2.4 thread API.
 - sockaddr_t replaces struct sockaddr_storage in DANOS code; interface
   address checks test the in_addr/in6_addr directly.
 - Removed the SOCK_CLOEXEC/SOCK_NONBLOCK fallbacks (2.4 dropped the checks).
 - DANOS bugs fixed on the way: uninitialised sockopt/auxopt passed to
   setsockopt (auxopt 0 disables PACKET_AUXDATA and the VLAN check),
   unbounded strncpy of track_route/track_pathmon names, a missing log
   argument, and a bool compared with PARAMETER_UNSET.
 


